<h2><span class="sec-num">2</span> Business Requirement</h2>
<h3>2.1 Requirement Statement</h3>
<p>Procurement needs a report that lists <strong>overdue purchase orders grouped by vendor</strong> for one <strong>company code</strong>. Users enter their criteria on a selection screen. The result appears in an interactive ALV grid, so buyers and supply-chain managers can see which vendors are late, by how many days, and how much open value is affected. They can then expedite or escalate.</p>

<h3>2.2 Business Objectives</h3>
<ul>
<li>See all late deliveries for each vendor and company code in one place.</li>
<li>Rank vendors by overdue open value and by days late, so expediting effort goes where it matters most.</li>
<li>Replace manual work in ME2M / ME2L and spreadsheet consolidation.</li>
<li>Support vendor-performance discussions with objective ageing buckets.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.3 Scope</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>In Scope</th><th>Out of Scope</th></tr>
<tr><td>Standard purchase orders (document category F)</td><td>Contracts, scheduling agreements, RFQs (BSTYP K / L / A)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Overdue checks at schedule-line level (delivery date vs key date)</td><td>Invoice / payment overdue status (handled by AP ageing)</td></tr>
<tr><td>One company code per run (mandatory)</td><td>Cross-company-code consolidation in a single run</td></tr>
<tr><td>Display in ALV, with export to Excel through standard ALV functions</td><td>Automatic vendor e-mails or reminder output (possible later phase)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Online and background execution (with a layout variant)</td><td>Changing POs (the report is read-only)</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>2.4 Users &amp; Frequency</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>User Group</th><th>Usage</th><th>Frequency</th></tr>
<tr><td>Buyers / Purchasing Group</td><td>Daily expediting list</td><td>Daily (online)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Procurement Manager</td><td>Vendor escalation, KPI review</td><td>Weekly</td></tr>
<tr><td>Supply Chain Planning</td><td>Material-availability risk</td><td>Ad hoc</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">3</span> Definitions &amp; Business Rules</h2>
<h3>3.1 Definition of "Overdue"</h3>
<div class="callout">A PO schedule line is <strong>overdue</strong> if <strong>all</strong> of these are true:
<ol>
<li>Header: <code>EKKO-BUKRS = P_BUKRS</code>, <code>EKKO-BSTYP = 'F'</code>, <code>EKKO-LOEKZ = space</code>.</li>
<li>Item: <code>EKPO-LOEKZ = space</code> (not deleted or blocked) and <code>EKPO-ELIKZ = space</code> (delivery not completed).</li>
<li>Schedule line: <code>EKET-EINDT &lt; P_KEYDT</code> (delivery date before the key date; default key date = today). Lines where <code>EINDT</code> is initial (00000000) are skipped.</li>
<li>Open quantity &gt; 0, where <code>Open Qty = EKET-MENGE − EKET-WEMNG</code>.</li>
<li>Days overdue ≥ <code>P_MINDAY</code> (default 1).</li>
</ol></div>

<h3>3.2 Calculated Fields</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Formula</th><th>Rule</th></tr>
<tr><td>Open Quantity</td><td>EKET-MENGE − EKET-WEMNG</td><td>Only rows with a result &gt; 0 are kept</td></tr>
<tr><td>Days Overdue</td><td>P_KEYDT − EKET-EINDT</td><td>Integer; if the result is negative, set to 0 and exclude</td></tr>
<tr><td>Open Value</td><td>Open Qty × EKPO-NETPR / EKPO-PEINH</td><td>If PEINH = 0, use 1. Result in the PO currency (EKKO-WAERS). Use a wide packed type (P LENGTH 15 DECIMALS 2) to avoid overflow</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ageing Bucket</td><td>Based on Days Overdue</td><td>1–30 · 31–60 · 61–90 · &gt;90 days</td></tr>
<tr><td>Traffic Light</td><td>Based on Ageing Bucket</td><td>Yellow 1–30 · Orange 31–60 · Red &gt;60</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>3.3 Key Business Rules</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>BR-01 Currency:</strong> Open values are never totalled across currencies. Vendor subtotals are built per vendor <em>and</em> per currency (EKKO-WAERS).</li>
<li><strong>BR-02 Granularity:</strong> The detail level is the schedule line (EBELN / EBELP / ETENR). One PO item can have several overdue schedule lines.</li>
<li><strong>BR-03 Vendor:</strong> The vendor is EKKO-LIFNR. The name comes from LFA1-NAME1. Vendors with a central posting block (LFA1-SPERR) or purchasing block (LFA1-SPERM) are still listed, with a "Blocked" indicator.</li>
<li><strong>BR-04 Number formats:</strong> EBELN and LIFNR are 10 characters and MATNR is 18 characters (ECC). They are shown with conversion exits (leading zeros suppressed).</li>
<li><strong>BR-05 Read-only:</strong> The report changes no data.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="sec-num">4</span> Selection Screen</h2>
<h3>4.1 Block 1 – Organisational Data</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Technical Name</th><th>Label</th><th>Type / Reference</th><th>Kind</th><th>Mandatory</th><th>Default</th></tr>
<tr><td>P_BUKRS</td><td>Company Code</td><td>EKKO-BUKRS (BUKRS, CHAR 4)</td><td>Parameter</td><td>Yes</td><td>User parameter BUK</td></tr>
<tr><td>S_EKORG</td><td>Purchasing Organization</td><td>EKKO-EKORG (EKORG, CHAR 4)</td><td>Select-option</td><td>No</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>S_EKGRP</td><td>Purchasing Group</td><td>EKKO-EKGRP (BKGRP, CHAR 3)</td><td>Select-option</td><td>No</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>S_WERKS</td><td>Plant</td><td>EKPO-WERKS (EWERK, CHAR 4)</td><td>Select-option</td><td>No</td><td>—</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>4.2 Block 2 – Document / Vendor Data</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Technical Name</th><th>Label</th><th>Type / Reference</th><th>Kind</th><th>Mandatory</th><th>Default</th></tr>
<tr><td>S_LIFNR</td><td>Vendor</td><td>EKKO-LIFNR (ELIFN, CHAR 10)</td><td>Select-option</td><td>No</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>S_EBELN</td><td>Purchasing Document</td><td>EKKO-EBELN (EBELN, CHAR 10)</td><td>Select-option</td><td>No</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>S_BSART</td><td>PO Document Type</td><td>EKKO-BSART (ESART, CHAR 4)</td><td>Select-option</td><td>No</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>S_MATNR</td><td>Material</td><td>EKPO-MATNR (MATNR, CHAR 18)</td><td>Select-option</td><td>No</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>S_BEDAT</td><td>PO Date</td><td>EKKO-BEDAT (EBDAT, DATS)</td><td>Select-option</td><td>No</td><td>—</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>4.3 Block 3 – Overdue Criteria &amp; Output</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Technical Name</th><th>Label</th><th>Type / Reference</th><th>Kind</th><th>Mandatory</th><th>Default</th></tr>
<tr><td>S_EINDT</td><td>Delivery Date</td><td>EKET-EINDT (EINDT, DATS)</td><td>Select-option</td><td>No</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>P_KEYDT</td><td>Key Date (overdue as of)</td><td>SY-DATUM (DATS)</td><td>Parameter</td><td>Yes</td><td>Today</td></tr>
<tr><td>P_MINDAY</td><td>Minimum Days Overdue</td><td>INT4 (0–9999)</td><td>Parameter</td><td>No</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>P_DETAIL / P_SUMM</td><td>Output: Detail (schedule lines) / Vendor Summary</td><td>Radio-button group</td><td>Radio</td><td>—</td><td>Detail</td></tr>
<tr><td>P_VARI</td><td>ALV Layout</td><td>SLIS_VARI / DISVARIANT-VARIANT</td><td>Parameter (F4 help)</td><td>No</td><td>User default layout</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="callout tip">Each organisational or master-data field uses its DDIC type (CHAR keys are never typed as dates). Only P_KEYDT, S_BEDAT and S_EINDT are date fields.</div>

<h3>4.4 Validation of Selection Criteria</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>#</th><th>Check</th><th>Event</th><th>Message Type</th><th>Message Text</th></tr>
<tr><td>V1</td><td>P_BUKRS exists in T001</td><td>AT SELECTION-SCREEN ON P_BUKRS</td><td>E</td><td>Company code &amp;1 does not exist</td></tr>
<tr><td>V2</td><td>User is authorised for at least one purchasing org in S_EKORG (M_BEST_EKO)</td><td>AT SELECTION-SCREEN</td><td>E</td><td>No authorization for purchasing organization &amp;1</td></tr>
<tr><td>V3</td><td>P_KEYDT is not initial</td><td>AT SELECTION-SCREEN ON P_KEYDT</td><td>E</td><td>Enter a valid key date</td></tr>
<tr><td>V4</td><td>P_MINDAY ≥ 0</td><td>AT SELECTION-SCREEN ON P_MINDAY</td><td>E</td><td>Minimum days overdue cannot be negative</td></tr>
<tr><td>V5</td><td>Upper bound of S_EINDT is ≤ P_KEYDT</td><td>AT SELECTION-SCREEN</td><td>W</td><td>Delivery dates after the key date are never overdue</td></tr>
<tr><td>V6</td><td>P_VARI layout exists for the report</td><td>AT SELECTION-SCREEN ON P_VARI</td><td>E</td><td>Layout &amp;1 does not exist</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">5</span> Data Sources</h2>
<h3>5.1 SAP Tables Read (verified against the target dictionary)</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Table</th><th>Description</th><th>Key Fields Used</th><th>Fields Read</th></tr>
<tr><td>EKKO</td><td>Purchasing Document Header</td><td>EBELN</td><td>EBELN, BUKRS, BSTYP, BSART, LOEKZ, LIFNR, EKORG, EKGRP, BEDAT, WAERS, ZTERM</td></tr>
<tr><td>EKPO</td><td>Purchasing Document Item</td><td>EBELN, EBELP</td><td>EBELP, LOEKZ, ELIKZ, MATNR, TXZ01, WERKS, LGORT, MENGE, MEINS, NETPR, PEINH, NETWR, MATKL</td></tr>
<tr><td>EKET</td><td>Schedule Lines</td><td>EBELN, EBELP, ETENR</td><td>ETENR, EINDT, MENGE, WEMNG</td></tr>
<tr><td>LFA1</td><td>Vendor Master (General)</td><td>LIFNR</td><td>NAME1, ORT01, LAND1, SPERR, SPERM</td></tr>
<tr><td>T001</td><td>Company Codes</td><td>BUKRS</td><td>BUTXT, WAERS (validation and header text)</td></tr>
<tr><td>T024</td><td>Purchasing Groups</td><td>EKGRP</td><td>EKNAM (buyer name, optional column)</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>5.2 Company Codes in the Target System (sample from T001)</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>BUKRS</th><th>Name</th><th>Currency</th><th>Country</th></tr>
<tr><td>1000</td><td>BestRun Germany</td><td>EUR</td><td>DE</td></tr>
<tr><td>1010</td><td>BestRun INDIA 1010</td><td>INR</td><td>IN</td></tr>
<tr><td>1710</td><td>BestRun INDIA</td><td>INR</td><td>IN</td></tr>
<tr><td>2000</td><td>BestRun UK</td><td>GBP</td><td>GB</td></tr>
<tr><td>2200</td><td>BestRun France</td><td>EUR</td><td>FR</td></tr>
<tr><td>0006</td><td>BestRun US INC New GL</td><td>USD</td><td>US</td></tr>
</table>
<p>The company codes use different local currencies (EUR, INR, GBP, USD, SGD). This is why rule BR-01 (no blending of currencies) is required.</p>

