s="nodeLabel "><p>Read vendor names from LFA1 for distinct LIFNR</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-I-17" transform="translate(448, 1251.78125)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-51" width="260" height="102"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -36)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="72"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Calculate days overdue, open value, ageing bucket, traffic light</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-J-19" transform="translate(448, 1426.8828125)"><polygon points="74.1015625,0 148.203125,-74.1015625 74.1015625,-148.203125 0,-74.1015625" class="label-container" transform="translate(-73.6015625, 74.1015625)"></polygon><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-47.1015625, -12)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="94.203125" height="24"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table-cell; white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Output mode</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-K-21" transform="translate(293, 1625.984375)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-51" width="260" height="102"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -36)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="72"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>ALV schedule-line list, sorted by vendor, subtotals per vendor and currency</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-L-23" transform="translate(603, 1625.984375)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-51" width="260" height="102"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -36)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="72"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Aggregate per vendor and currency, then show ALV summary</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></svg></figure>

<h3>6.1 Step-by-Step Logic</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Initialisation:</strong> Set P_KEYDT = SY-DATUM, P_MINDAY = 1, read the default ALV layout, and set frame titles.</li>
<li><strong>Data selection (single DB round trip):</strong> Use an INNER JOIN EKKO → EKPO (EBELN) → EKET (EBELN, EBELP) with these conditions: <code>EKKO-BUKRS = P_BUKRS</code>, <code>BSTYP = 'F'</code>, <code>EKKO-LOEKZ = space</code>, <code>EKPO-LOEKZ = space</code>, <code>EKPO-ELIKZ = space</code>, <code>EKET-EINDT &lt; P_KEYDT</code>, <code>EKET-EINDT &lt;&gt; '00000000'</code>, and all select-options. Select only the columns listed in §5.1 (no SELECT *).</li>
<li><strong>Open-quantity filter:</strong> In ABAP, drop rows where MENGE − WEMNG ≤ 0.</li>
<li><strong>Authorization filter:</strong> Remove rows the user is not allowed to display (see §8) and count them for the information message.</li>
<li><strong>Vendor master:</strong> If the result is not empty, read LFA1 with FOR ALL ENTRIES on the distinct LIFNR values into a hashed table, then do key reads (no SELECT inside a LOOP).</li>
<li><strong>Calculations:</strong> Calculate the fields in §3.2. Guard every division (PEINH = 0 → 1). Ignore negative day values.</li>
<li><strong>Min-days filter:</strong> Drop rows where Days Overdue &lt; P_MINDAY.</li>
<li><strong>Summary mode:</strong> Group by LIFNR + WAERS. Output: number of POs, number of schedule lines, total open value, maximum days overdue, average days overdue, and open value per ageing bucket.</li>
<li><strong>Output:</strong> Show the result in CL_SALV_TABLE (see §7).</li>
</ol>

<h3>6.2 Performance Considerations</h3>
<ul>
<li>The company code is mandatory, so the header read is always restricted. EKET has no index on EINDT, so filtering on EINDT through the join is acceptable when BUKRS / EKORG are restricted.</li>
<li>Expected volume: ≤ 50,000 schedule lines per company code. Recommend running in background for full company codes with no other restriction.</li>
<li>Use FOR ALL ENTRIES only after an IS NOT INITIAL check on the driver table.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="sec-num">7</span> Output – ALV Layout</h2>
<h3>7.1 Detail Mode (default)</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>#</th><th>Column</th><th>Source</th><th>Sort / Subtotal</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Traffic Light</td><td>Calculated</td><td>—</td><td>Icon / colour by ageing bucket</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Vendor</td><td>EKKO-LIFNR</td><td>Sort 1, subtotal</td><td>Hotspot → XK03 (display vendor)</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Vendor Name</td><td>LFA1-NAME1</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>Blocked</td><td>LFA1-SPERR / SPERM</td><td>—</td><td>Checkbox display</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>Currency</td><td>EKKO-WAERS</td><td>Sort 2, subtotal</td><td>Reference for open value</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>Purchasing Document</td><td>EKKO-EBELN</td><td>Sort 3</td><td>Hotspot → ME23N</td></tr>
<tr><td>7</td><td>Item</td><td>EKPO-EBELP</td><td>Sort 4</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>8</td><td>Schedule Line</td><td>EKET-ETENR</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>9</td><td>Document Type</td><td>EKKO-BSART</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>10</td><td>Purch. Org / Group</td><td>EKKO-EKORG / EKGRP</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>11</td><td>Plant</td><td>EKPO-WERKS</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>12</td><td>Material / Short Text</td><td>EKPO-MATNR / TXZ01</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>13</td><td>PO Date</td><td>EKKO-BEDAT</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>14</td><td>Delivery Date</td><td>EKET-EINDT</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>15</td><td>Scheduled Qty</td><td>EKET-MENGE</td><td>—</td><td>Unit EKPO-MEINS</td></tr>
<tr><td>16</td><td>Received Qty</td><td>EKET-WEMNG</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>17</td><td>Open Qty</td><td>Calculated</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>18</td><td>Net Price / Price Unit</td><td>EKPO-NETPR / PEINH</td><td>—</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>19</td><td>Open Value</td><td>Calculated</td><td>Sum</td><td>Per currency only</td></tr>
<tr><td>20</td><td>Days Overdue</td><td>Calculated</td><td>Max on subtotal</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>21</td><td>Ageing Bucket</td><td>Calculated</td><td>—</td><td>Text 1–30 / 31–60 / 61–90 / &gt;90</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>7.2 Summary Mode</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Vendor / Name / Currency</td><td>Grouping keys</td></tr>
<tr><td>No. of POs / No. of Schedule Lines</td><td>Distinct EBELN count / row count</td></tr>
<tr><td>Total Open Value</td><td>Sum of the open value (per currency)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Value 1–30 / 31–60 / 61–90 / &gt;90</td><td>Open value per ageing bucket</td></tr>
<tr><td>Max / Avg Days Overdue</td><td>Worst and average lateness</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Default sort in summary mode: Total Open Value, descending (the worst vendors appear first).</p>

<h3>7.3 ALV Features</h3>
<ul>
<li>Standard toolbar (sort, filter, sum, Excel export, layout save) through <code>CL_SALV_TABLE</code> (classic SAP GUI ALV, compatible with SAP_BASIS 740).</li>
<li>Column headers come from the DDIC data-element texts. Only the calculated columns have explicit short, medium and long texts.</li>
<li>Header line: Company Code + Name (T001-BUTXT), Key Date, number of records.</li>
<li>Hotspots: EBELN → ME23N, LIFNR → XK03 (display only).</li>
<li>Saving user-specific and global layouts is allowed.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="sec-num">8</span> Authorization Requirements</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Auth Object</th><th>Field(s)</th><th>Value</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td>S_TCODE</td><td>TCD</td><td>ZMM_OVDPO</td><td>Start the transaction</td></tr>
<tr><td>M_BEST_EKO</td><td>EKORG, ACTVT</td><td>Purch. org, 03</td><td>Display POs per purchasing organization</td></tr>
<tr><td>M_BEST_EKG</td><td>EKGRP, ACTVT</td><td>Purch. group, 03</td><td>Display POs per purchasing group</td></tr>
<tr><td>M_BEST_WRK</td><td>WERKS, ACTVT</td><td>Plant, 03</td><td>Display POs per plant</td></tr>
<tr><td>M_BEST_BSA</td><td>BSART, ACTVT</td><td>Doc type, 03</td><td>Display POs per document type</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Rows the user is not authorised for are removed without an error. At the end, an information message says how many rows were excluded.</p>

<h2><span class="sec-num">9</span> Messages</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>No.</th><th>Type</th><th>Text</th><th>When</th></tr>
<tr><td>001</td><td>E</td><td>Company code &amp;1 does not exist</td><td>V1</td></tr>
<tr><td>002</td><td>E</td><td>No authorization for purchasing organization &amp;1</td><td>V2</td></tr>
<tr><td>003</td><td>E</td><td>Enter a valid key date</td><td>V3</td></tr>
<tr><td>004</td><td>E</td><td>Minimum days overdue cannot be negative</td><td>V4</td></tr>
<tr><td>005</td><td>W</td><td>Delivery dates after the key date are never overdue</td><td>V5</td></tr>
<tr><td>006</td><td>S</td><td>No overdue purchase orders found for the selection</td><td>Empty result</td></tr>
<tr><td>007</td><td>I</td><td>&amp;1 records hidden due to missing authorization</td><td>After the authorization filter</td></tr>
<tr><td>008</td><td>E</td><td>Layout &amp;1 does not exist</td><td>V6</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Proposed message class: <strong>ZMM_OVDPO</strong>.</p>

<h2><span class="sec-num">10</span> Error Handling</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Situation</th><th>Handling</th><th>What the User Sees</th></tr>
<tr><td>No data selected</td><td>Exit before the ALV is built</td><td>Message 006 (status bar)</td></tr>
<tr><td>ALV factory fails</td><td>CATCH cx_salv_msg</td><td>Error message, report ends</td></tr>
<tr><td>Column config fails</td><td>CATCH cx_salv_not_found (does not stop the report)</td><td>Warning; ALV is still shown</td></tr>
<tr><td>Arithmetic overflow / division</td><td>PEINH guard, wide packed type, TRY/CATCH cx_sy_arithmetic_error</td><td>Row flagged; processing continues</td></tr>
<tr><td>Initial delivery date</td><td>Excluded at selection</td><td>Not listed (never shown as "infinitely overdue")</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">11</span> Technical Design Notes (for the TS)</h2>
<ul>
<li>One executable program with local classes (no FORM/PERFORM): <code>lcl_report</code> (orchestration), <code>lif_data_access</code> / <code>lcl_db_access</code> (SELECT seam), <code>lcl_alv</code> (display).</li>
<li>START-OF-SELECTION stays thin and only orchestrates. The business logic is in methods that ABAP Unit can test (a fake data-access class supplies edge-case rows; CL_OSQL_TEST_ENVIRONMENT is not available on SAP_BASIS 740).</li>
<li>Structure fields that receive table columns are typed <code>TYPE &lt;table&gt;-&lt;field&gt;</code>. Totals use P LENGTH 15 DECIMALS 2.</li>
<li>Background run supported: the ALV prints as a spool list. The layout is taken from P_VARI.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="sec-num">12</span> Test Scenarios</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>ID</th><th>Type</th><th>Scenario</th><th>Input</th><th>Expected Result</th></tr>
<tr><td>T01</td><td>Positive</td><td>Overdue PO lines exist for the company code</td><td>P_BUKRS = 1000, key date = today</td><td>ALV lists overdue schedule lines, grouped by vendor with subtotals per currency</td></tr>
<tr><td>T02</td><td>Positive</td><td>Summary mode</td><td>As T01 + P_SUMM</td><td>One row per vendor and currency, sorted by open value descending</td></tr>
<tr><td>T03</td><td>Positive</td><td>Partially received line</td><td>Line with MENGE 100, WEMNG 40</td><td>Open Qty = 60; open value = 60 × NETPR / PEINH</td></tr>
<tr><td>T04</td><td>Negative</td><td>Invalid company code</td><td>P_BUKRS = 9999</td><td>Error 001; report does not run</td></tr>
<tr><td>T05</td><td>Negative</td><td>Fully delivered item</td><td>EKPO-ELIKZ = X</td><td>Line not listed</td></tr>
<tr><td>T06</td><td>Negative</td><td>Deleted item</td><td>EKPO-LOEKZ = L</td><td>Line not listed</td></tr>
<tr><td>T07</td><td>Boundary</td><td>Delivery date = key date</td><td>EINDT = P_KEYDT</td><td>Not overdue; not listed</td></tr>
<tr><td>T08</td><td>Boundary</td><td>Ageing bucket edges</td><td>Days overdue 30 / 31 / 60 / 61 / 90 / 91</td><td>Correct bucket for each value</td></tr>
<tr><td>T09</td><td>Boundary</td><td>Price unit 0</td><td>PEINH = 0</td><td>Treated as 1; no dump</td></tr>
<tr><td>T10</td><td>Edge</td><td>Vendor with POs in two currencies</td><td>EUR + USD POs</td><td>Two separate subtotals; no blended total</td></tr>
<tr><td>T11</td><td>Edge</td><td>No overdue data</td><td>Future key-date filter</td><td>Message 006</td></tr>
<tr><td>T12</td><td>Authorization</td><td>User without M_BEST_EKO for one purchasing org</td><td>Restricted test user</td><td>Those rows are hidden; message 007</td></tr>
<tr><td>T13</td><td>Reconciliation</td><td>Compare with standard</td><td>Same PO in ME2L / ME2M (selection parameter WE101)</td><td>Open quantities match the standard report</td></tr>
<tr><td>T14</td><td>Performance</td><td>Full company code in background</td><td>P_BUKRS only</td><td>Finishes within agreed SLA (TBD, e.g. &lt; 5 min)</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">13</span> Assumptions, Dependencies &amp; Open Points</h2>
<h3>13.1 Assumptions</h3>
<ul>
<li>"Overdue" means a late <em>delivery</em> (goods receipt), not a late invoice or payment.</li>
<li>The schedule-line delivery date (EKET-EINDT) is the agreed due date. The statistical date (SLFDT) is not used.</li>
<li>The goods-receipt quantity on the schedule line (EKET-WEMNG) is maintained reliably.</li>
</ul>
<h3>13.2 Open Points for Business Sign-off</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>#</th><th>Question</th><th>Owner</th><th>Status</th></tr>
<tr><td>OP-1</td><td>Include stock transport orders (document type UB) or exclude them by default?</td><td>Procurement</td><td>Open</td></tr>
<tr><td>OP-2</td><td>Add a grace period (e.g. GR processing time EKPO-WEBAZ) before a line counts as overdue?</td><td>Procurement</td><td>Open</td></tr>
<tr><td>OP-3</td><td>Should the open value also be converted to company-code currency, as an additional column?</td><td>Finance</td><td>Open</td></tr>
<tr><td>OP-4</td><td>Performance SLA for background runs</td><td>IT / Basis</td><td>Open</td></tr>
<tr><td>OP-5</td><td>Is vendor e-mail / reminder output needed in a later phase?</td><td>Procurement</td><td>Open</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">14</span> Standard SAP Alternatives Considered</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Standard Option</th><th>Gap</th></tr>
<tr><td>ME2M / ME2L / ME2N with parameter WE101</td><td>No overdue-day calculation, no ageing buckets, no vendor summary with per-currency subtotals</td></tr>
<tr><td>ME91F (Urging / reminders)</td><td>Focuses on output and reminders, not an analytical overview by vendor</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vendor evaluation (ME61 / ME6H)</td><td>Gives scores, not an operational list of open late lines</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Conclusion: a custom report is justified. The design is read-only and uses standard tables only (classic Level B, compatible with ECC / SAP_BASIS 740 and S/4HANA on-premise).</p>
